Always consult /docs before major recommendations.
Treat business-context/ and resource-library/ as read-only reference inputs.
If guidance is derived from those references, state it is "informed by the reference library" without naming files.
Never invent product requirements; ask or log an open question in QUESTIONS.md.
Maintain DECISIONS.md, ASSUMPTIONS.md, QUESTIONS.md continuously.
Prefer small, reviewable changes over large rewrites.
Keep scope changes reflected in SCOPE.md and DECISIONS.md.
Non-negotiables: consult /docs first; never name filenames from reference folders; log ambiguity to QUESTIONS.md; require PROJECT.md + SCOPE.md + docs/03-requirements/REQUIREMENTS.md before product code.